  "id": "COMPOUND:24945 - PROTEIN:4915",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which (16S)-21-methyl-18-oxa-1,11-diazahexacyclo[11.8.0.02,16.04,12.05,10.015,20]henicosa-4(12),5,7,9-tetraen-17-ol interacts with Replicase polyprotein 1ab. This compound appears to act as a target of multiple compounds, including Petroraspailyne B1, 5-Hydroxy-2-Methylchromone-7-O-Rutinoside, and (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan, all of which are known to target Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like. This indicates that the compound may inhibit the enzyme, which in turn could affect the replication of the target protein. The evidence supports a possible role of this compound in modulating the activity of Replicase polyprotein 1ab, potentially through the inhibition of Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like. The mechanism is supported by the presence of multiple compounds with distinct but related targets, suggesting a possible pathway of action that is consistent with the observed interactions.",
